<given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hurd</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Garland</surname><given-names>T</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Selective breeding for a behavioral trait changes digit ratio.</article-title><source>PloS One</source><volume>3(9)</volume><fpage>e2316</fpage><comment>doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0003216</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18509458</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005801-Hurd1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hurd</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bailey</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gongal</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yan</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Greer</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>The manliness of mice: Intrauterine position effects on digit ratio and anogenital distance.</article-title><source>Arch Sex Behav</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18080736</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005801-Sokal1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sokal</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rohlf</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1995</year><source>Biometry, 3<sup>rd</sup> ed</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>WH Freeman</publisher-name><fpage>880</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005801-Cohen1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1988</year><source>Statistical power analysis for the behavioral sciences. 2<sup>nd</sup> ed</source><pub